WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.092 --> 00:00:07.292
Jack Gibson hurried out of the car and ran to the swimming pool.

2
00:00:07.294 --> 00:00:13.786
"Awesome!" he thought. The pool at the apartment complex was large with two lap lanes.

3
00:00:13.787 --> 00:00:21.626
Best of all, it was only steps away from his family's new apartment. He was going to love California!

4
00:00:21.627 --> 00:00:24.064
"Jack!" Luke called out.

5
00:00:24.066 --> 00:00:25.940
Jack didn't turn around.

6
00:00:25.941 --> 00:00:32.258
He loved his four-year-old brother, but the last three days in the car with him had felt like three years.

7
00:00:32.259 --> 00:00:36.517
He couldn't wait to get to his new bedroom and lock the door.

8
00:00:36.518 --> 00:00:39.268
"Jack!" Luke yelled louder.

9
00:00:39.269 --> 00:00:43.500
Jack turned around and scowled. "What?"

10
00:00:43.501 --> 00:00:48.004
"Mommy and Daddy said to bring stuff to our new apartment."

11
00:00:48.005 --> 00:00:59.429
Jack walked back to the car and took a bag of clothes from the trunk. Fortunately, his dad had moved the furniture in the week before.

12
00:00:59.430 --> 00:01:10.997
Jack and his family headed to their new apartment. Inside, Jack saw it was tiny, less than half the size of their house back in Oklahoma.

13
00:01:10.998 --> 00:01:14.914
But that was okay. Their old house didn't have a pool.

14
00:01:14.915 --> 00:01:17.462
"Where's my bedroom?" Jack asked.

15
00:01:17.463 --> 00:01:20.230
He saw his parents frown at each other.

16
00:01:20.231 --> 00:01:24.356
"Um . . . we didn't want you to worry," his mother mumbled.

17
00:01:24.357 --> 00:01:27.323
"Worry about what?" Jack asked.

18
00:01:27.324 --> 00:01:30.113
"You and Luke will be sharing a room."

19
00:01:30.114 --> 00:01:33.139
"Yay!" Luke yelled.

20
00:01:33.140 --> 00:01:41.053
"Ugh," Jack muttered. Fourteen-year-olds were not supposed to share bedrooms with four-year-olds.

21
00:01:41.054 --> 00:01:44.945
"California's housing prices are much higher than Oklahoma's.

22
00:01:44.946 --> 00:01:50.301
We couldn't afford a bigger place, especially one with a pool," his father said.

23
00:01:50.302 --> 00:01:59.866
Jack walked into the bedroom. It had just enough room for two twin beds, a small dresser, and a tiny closet.

24
00:01:59.867 --> 00:02:05.951
On the other side of the wall, in the next apartment, a popular song from the Long-Hair Boys band was playing:

25
00:02:05.952 --> 00:02:22.334
"Baby, don't you see. You're my destiny."

26
00:02:22.335 --> 00:02:28.675
Jack rolled his eyes. Whoever lived next door had horrible taste in music.

27
00:02:28.676 --> 00:02:44.254
Luke sang along, off-key: "'Listen to my pleas. You're the one for me. Ooh, baby, baby, baby. Ooh, baby, baby, baby.'"

28
00:02:44.255 --> 00:02:52.582
Jack sank down on one of the beds. The only good thing about this apartment was the swimming pool.

29
00:02:52.583 --> 00:03:00.233
He looked at his parents, who stood in the doorway. "Can I go to the pool? I need to be ready for swim team practice tomorrow."

30
00:03:00.234 --> 00:03:04.393
"You need to unpack your things," his mother said.

31
00:03:04.394 --> 00:03:11.207
Jack grinned and held up something. "Look—I already unpacked a towel and my swimsuit!"

32
00:03:11.208 --> 00:03:13.020
His parents smiled.

33
00:03:13.022 --> 00:03:18.799
"Don't stay at the pool too long," his mom said. "You have a lot to do."

34
00:03:18.800 --> 00:03:20.925
"Thanks!" Jack exclaimed.

35
00:03:20.926 --> 00:03:28.055
As he rushed toward the pool, a voice rang out. "Slow down, young man!"

36
00:03:28.056 --> 00:03:37.206
Jack halted. An older woman sat in a lounge chair. She was built like a linebacker and wrinkled like a raisin.

37
00:03:37.207 --> 00:03:42.113
"It's rude to stare," she said with a scowl.

38
00:03:42.114 --> 00:03:49.943
"Sorry." Jack threw his towel onto a chair and dived into the pool.

39
00:03:49.944 --> 00:03:56.442
There were only a couple of other swimmers. Ahh. The water temperature was perfect.

40
00:03:56.443 --> 00:03:59.670
"Don't splash!" the old woman yelled.

41
00:03:59.671 --> 00:04:07.261
Jack tried to ignore her. He swam the breaststroke across the pool.

42
00:04:07.262 --> 00:04:16.176
He'd been the best at breaststroke on his team in Oklahoma, and at freestyle too. He hoped he'd be the best on the team here too.

43
00:04:16.177 --> 00:04:20.498
Now that he had a pool, he could practice more than ever.

44
00:04:20.499 --> 00:04:26.164
"You're raising your head too high. It's slowing you down," the old woman snapped.

45
00:04:26.165 --> 00:04:28.485
Jack ignored her and kept swimming.

46
00:04:28.486 --> 00:04:34.387
"And cup your hands when they enter the water!"

47
00:04:34.388 --> 00:04:40.567
Jack didn't even glance her way.

48
00:04:40.568 --> 00:04:50.641
Someone started swimming in the other lap lane. He looked over. A girl about his age was doing the backstroke.

49
00:04:50.642 --> 00:04:57.142
He swam over to her and flashed a smile. "Hey, I'm Jack. I just moved here today."

50
00:04:57.143 --> 00:05:10.203
"Welcome. I'm Laura." She dog-paddled next to him. She was very cute, with brown eyes, freckles, and a long, dark ponytail.

51
00:05:10.204 --> 00:05:15.127
"The only thing better than swimming," Jack thought, "is swimming with a cute girl!"

52
00:05:15.128 --> 00:05:17.386
"Do you like living here?" he asked.

53
00:05:17.387 --> 00:05:21.628
"I do. The pool is awesome, and our neighbors are nice."

54
00:05:21.629 --> 00:05:25.535
"Hey! Keep the noise down," the old woman said.

55
00:05:25.536 --> 00:05:28.461
"You call that nice?" Jack muttered.

56
00:05:28.462 --> 00:05:33.775
Laura smiled politely at the woman. "Hello, I'm Laura Perez."

57
00:05:33.776 --> 00:05:43.349
The woman didn't smile back. "Ellen Wilson. Call me Mrs. Wilson. Or ma'am. I moved here three days ago."

58
00:05:43.350 --> 00:05:47.195
"Welcome to Sunnyside Apartments, ma'am," Laura said.

59
00:05:47.196 --> 00:05:53.098
"I'm Jack Gibson." Jack smiled at the old lady, just to show Laura he was a friendly guy.

60
00:05:53.099 --> 00:05:55.443
Mrs. Wilson scowled at him.

61
00:05:55.444 --> 00:05:58.849
"Want to race across the pool?" Jack asked Laura.

62
00:05:58.850 --> 00:06:01.100
Laura grinned. "Sure."

63
00:06:01.101 --> 00:06:03.824
Jack smiled for real now.

64
00:06:03.825 --> 00:06:11.323
Laura would be amazed by his speed. He wouldn't swim too fast, just enough to beat her by five meters or so.

65
00:06:11.324 --> 00:06:18.417
He didn't want to humiliate her. Afterward, he could give pointers on her technique—not in a mean way like Mrs. Wilson.

66
00:06:18.418 --> 00:06:22.995
His way would be helpful, and Laura would appreciate it.

67
00:06:22.996 --> 00:06:26.973
"I'll referee the race," Mrs. Wilson said.

68
00:06:26.974 --> 00:06:29.240
"Great!" Laura exclaimed.

69
00:06:29.241 --> 00:06:37.328
"Great," Jack muttered. He and Laura got out of the water and stood at the edge of the pool.

70
00:06:37.329 --> 00:06:44.804
"Young man, I hope you display better form in freestyle than in the breaststroke," Mrs. Wilson said.

71
00:06:44.805 --> 00:06:49.578
Jack forced himself to smile politely. "I'll do my best."

72
00:06:49.579 --> 00:06:52.797
"Take your mark," Mrs. Wilson said.

73
00:06:52.798 --> 00:06:55.892
Jack and Laura got into diving positions.

74
00:06:55.893 --> 00:06:59.717
"Go!" Mrs. Wilson yelled.

75
00:06:59.718 --> 00:07:07.883
Jack got off to a quick start, entering the water with just a slight splash.

76
00:07:07.884 --> 00:07:13.112
He pushed through the water with forceful strokes and strong scissors kicks.

77
00:07:13.113 --> 00:07:23.859
He reminded himself not to get too far ahead of Laura. He glanced at her lane. She was swimming right next to him.

78
00:07:23.860 --> 00:07:28.141
"Actually," he realized, "she might be a little ahead of me."

79
00:07:28.142 --> 00:07:31.916
"Focus, Jack!" Mrs. Wilson called out.

80
00:07:31.917 --> 00:07:38.336
Jack missed a breath, which made him lose more focus, and Laura quickly pulled ahead of him.

81
00:07:38.337 --> 00:07:46.988
Jack sped up, suddenly swimming as if he were racing for a spot on the Olympic team.

82
00:07:46.989 --> 00:07:50.826
But Laura touched the wall of the pool first.

83
00:07:50.827 --> 00:08:01.487
"Laura is the winner," Mrs. Wilson said. "The clear winner. That makes Jack the clear loser."

84
00:08:01.488 --> 00:08:07.216
Laura smiled at Jack. "Good race. That was fun."

85
00:08:07.217 --> 00:08:12.920
He nodded but didn't smile back. It was a terrible race!

86
00:08:12.921 --> 00:08:19.220
In Oklahoma he'd never been beaten by a girl. He'd hardly ever been beaten by anyone.

87
00:08:19.221 --> 00:08:22.908
"Good freestyle form," Mrs. Wilson said.

88
00:08:22.910 --> 00:08:25.202
"Thanks," Jack replied.

89
00:08:25.203 --> 00:08:34.153
"I was talking to Laura," Mrs. Wilson said. "Young man, your breathing was completely off and your legs were a mile apart.

90
00:08:34.154 --> 00:08:36.977
If you're going to be a swimmer, you—"

91
00:08:36.978 --> 00:08:39.854
Splash!

92
00:08:39.855 --> 00:08:48.705
Jack dived back into the pool before she was finished speaking.

